# control_podium/server_bridge/.ssh.secret — Pi deploy credentials
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Copy this file to `.ssh.secret` (gitignored) and fill in the values
# for your Raspberry Pi. Read by `server_bridge.deploy` and
# `firmware.deploy` to ssh / rsync / esptool the bridge code +
# firmware to the Pi.
#
# Required:
#   HOST          IPv4 or hostname of the Pi on the LAN
#   USER          login on the Pi (typically `titanic`)
#   INSTALL_ROOT  absolute path where the bridge is installed on the
#                 Pi (e.g. /opt/titanic-bridge)
#
# Optional:
#   PORT          ssh port (defaults to 22)
#   PASSWORD      enables sshpass-backed login + sudo. Leave unset to
#                 use ssh keys + NOPASSWD sudo.
#   ENGINE_URL    if set, the systemd unit on the Pi gets
#                 `--engine <url>` baked in. Otherwise the bridge
#                 reads `engine.url` from `.config.bridge.yaml`.
#
# Shell-style KEY=VALUE lines. Quote values containing spaces.

# HOST=<your-pi-lan-ip-or-hostname>
# USER=titanic
# PORT=22
# INSTALL_ROOT=/opt/titanic-bridge
# PASSWORD=<raspi-password>
# ENGINE_URL=http://<engine-lan-ip-or-hostname>:6968
